        "event": "Hydrologic Outlook",
        "headline": "Hydrologic Outlook issued September 12 at 11:05AM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "ESFAFG\n\n...Locations Impacted...\nFairbanks Metro Area-Two Rivers\n\nAfter recent rains, the Chena River is expected to rise through\nMonday afternoon and crest around 22.5 ft below Moose Creek Dam. This\nlevel would be right at action stage and those near or along the\nriver will notice that the Chena is at bankfull. We do not anticipate\nflooding from this, but it is possible that groundwater levels rise,\nresulting in localized water pooling in typical low lying and poor\ndrainage areas.\n\nFor more inf",
